  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"0.1.0\"\n\npackage:\n  name: pacman\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://gitlab.com/drti/pacman/-/archive/v${{ version }}/pacman-v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 3baba5b25bfed66bb49e20186192c6ac0ea75b8b1ba0932ed347449d29f7adb9\n  patches:\n    - 0001-install-python-extension-into-site-packages.patch\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  skip: osx and x86_64\n  dynamic_linking:\n    rpath_allowlist:\n      - $ORIGIN\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ compiler('cxx') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - cmake\n    - ninja\n  host:\n    - if: osx\n      then: llvm-openmp\n    - arborx >=2.1\n    - kokkos >=5.2\n    - kokkos-kernels >=5.2\n    - numpy\n    - pybind11 >=3\n    - python\n  run:\n    - arborx >=2.1\n    - kokkos >=5\n    - kokkos-kernels >=5\n    - numpy\n    - python\n\ntests:\n  - python:\n      imports:\n        - pacman\n  - script:\n      - if: unix\n        then: test -f $PREFIX/lib/cmake/PACMAN/PACMANConfig.cmake\n        else: if exist %LIBRARY_PREFIX%\\lib\\cmake\\PACMAN\\PACMANConfig.cmake (exit 0) else (exit 1)\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://gitlab.com/drti/pacman\n  summary: Portable algorithms for coupling, mapping, and adaptive interpolation\n  description: PACMAN is a C++ library with Python and Fortran bindings for portable coupling, mapping, and adaptive interpolation of scientific data.\n  license: BSD-3-Clause\n  license_file: LICENSE\n  documentation: https://drti.gitlab.io/pacman/\n  repository: https://gitlab.com/drti/pacman\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - fbordeu\n    - messahelramzi\n",
